ABOUT ROCKET LAB
&gt;
Rocket Lab is the end-to-end space company building rockets, spacecraft, and critical subsystems that keep the world connected, protected, expand humanity&#x27;s reach to the Moon, Mars, and beyond. We move fast, build real hardware for meaningful missions, and make the impossible routine. Come shape the future with us.
&gt;
&gt; SPACE SYSTEMS
&gt;
Rocket Lab&#x27;s Space Systems team is responsible for every satellite and satellite component made by Rocket Lab: from complete satellites destined for missions to the Moon and Mars, to the individual components and subsystems that make up a satellite like solar panels, flight software, reaction wheels and star trackers, separation systems, radios, and more. Our Space Systems team is made up of engineers, technicians, and designers who design, create, and put together our own satellites for missions across the commercial, government, and defense sectors, or who build and assemble satellite hardware and software that supports other satellite missions.
&gt;
RADAR PHASED ARRAY ENGINEER I
&gt;
Based at Rocket Lab&#x27;s global headquarters in Long Beach, CA, the Radar Phased Array Engineer I is responsible for the development of new RF products and systems (including Rocket Lab&#x27;s phased arrays) and assessment of COTS components. The RF Phased Array Engineer II will model and simulate antenna performance for current programs and proposals. The successful candidate will have a strong understanding of antennas at the component and system level and will thrive in a fast-paced, dynamic environment.
&gt;
WHAT YOU&#x27;LL GET TO DO:
&gt;
Product Development
&gt;
Support end to end efforts including architecture design, prototyping, integration, test, and flight development - Ensure key design decisions and developments are in alignment with product / system needs
&gt;
Model and simulate array performance
&gt;
Work alongside an interdisciplinary team of RF, digital, power, mechanical, thermal, and structural engineers
&gt;
Support transition developments from…

Celonis is the trusted platform to industrialize Enterprise AI. At our core is the Celonis Context Model - which combines process data, business knowledge, and intelligence into a living digital twin of the enterprise that AI can actually understand, turning AI&#x27;s operational blind spots into operational clarity. World&#x27;s leading companies trust Celonis and its global ecosystem of partners to make their AI agents, people, systems, and processes work together, achieving transformational outcomes. We believe there&#x27;s a massive opportunity to unlock global productivity and sustainability by giving AI the context to understand how every business process really works. Join our mission to make processes work for people, companies, and the planet.
&gt;
&gt; The Team:
&gt;
Our team, Agentic Customer Journey, is part of the Chief Customer Officer (CCO) organization. We are rebuilding how Celonis wins, delivers and grows customer relationships with AI agents. We design the methods and frameworks behind our value journey, from first discovery to realized value. Then we turn them into AI solutions that our Value Engineering and Services teams use every day. We work closely with Product, Engineering and senior leadership. We are expert generalists: equally comfortable building an agent workflow, structuring a value framework and presenting to executives.
&gt;
The Role:
&gt;
You will build AI solutions that automate and improve steps of our customer journey, plus the methodology that makes them work. You will take a use case from problem to working prototype: understand how teams work today, define the target process, build the solution, test it with real users and measure the impact. You will work with go-to-market (GTM) teams (Sales, Value Engineering, Services) and Product &amp; Engineering.
&gt;
The work you&#x27;ll do:
&gt;
Design, build and improve AI agents and assistants (LLM-based workflows, prompt chains, tool integrations). They will automate steps such as account research, meeting preparation,…

About Charles River Associates
&gt;
Charles River Associates is a leading global consulting firm that provides economic, financial, and business management expertise to major law firms, corporations and governments around the world. CRA advises clients on economic and financial matters pertaining to litigation and regulatory proceedings, and guides corporations through critical business strategy and performance-related issues. Since 1965, clients have engaged CRA for its combination of industry experience and rigorous, fact-based analysis that provide clients with clear, implementable solutions to complex business concerns.
&gt;
Position Overview
&gt;
CRA&#x27;s European Competition practice specialises in providing economic advice on matters of competition policy and regulation. We assist firms and their legal advisors in all types of competition proceedings before competition authorities and courts: mergers and acquisitions, abuse of dominance allegations, cartels, restrictive commercial agreements, market investigations, litigation and disputes, intellectual property or state aid. We also provide advice to regulatory authorities in similar matters. We also provide advice to firms involved in sector inquiries, and offer assistance on the estimation effects of damages in cartel cases, international arbitration and intellectual property disputes.
&gt;
We have played a key role in many cases that have shaped European competition policy in recent years: from aerospace to software, and manufacturing to transportation. More recently, we have been at the forefront of economic thinking in antitrust investigations and regulation in the tech sector.
&gt;
This paid internship mirrors our full-time analyst role. Interns work closely with senior staff on projects across a variety of industries, and will give Interns a greater understanding of what it is like to work as an economist at CRA. The internship duration is usually three to six months (flexible) with flexible start dates throughout…

The role: What&#x27;s in the Box
&gt;
We are looking for a Culinary Intern for our fast growing product team in Amsterdam. Working on the culinary team, you provide recipe testing support and give tasting feedback to help shape the meals customers receive every week.
Factor is a quickly growing brand within the HelloFresh Group. With ambitious product expansion plans, our culinary team is testing and launching multiple new meals every week from our test kitchen in the Amsterdam office. We&#x27;re seeking a Culinary Intern with a passion for food to help us accelerate this growth and delight our customers with delicious and healthy new recipes. On a small and dynamic team, this role has the opportunity to have a significant impact on our weekly menu and customer experience.
&gt;
What you&#x27;ll do: The Recipe
&gt;
Organize test kitchen ingredients, placing reorders when inventory is low, shopping weekly fresh items, and supporting R&amp;D chefs with ingredient prep for recipe testing
&gt;
Test assigned recipes, cooking components of meals and presenting them at team tastings. Document feedback and update recipes in development tool
&gt;
Ensure recipe accuracy and completeness for newly onboarded meals and existing recipes, updating and cross-checking as needed
&gt;
Take on the challenge of creating structure and clear processes within a large amount of product content across multiple languages and markets.
&gt;
Develop and be supported in strengthening your communication and presentation skills, while working on cross-functional team projects with different (international) personalities.
&gt;
Develop a structured way of working and support the product department in coordinating their administrative tasks, and documenting the processes created.
&gt;
What you&#x27;ll bring: The Ingredients
&gt;
Fluent in English
&gt;
Interested in culinary product development
&gt;
You don&#x27;t shy away from uncertainty and know to perform in a fast-pace environment
&gt;
Flexibility and adaptability to changing priorities, tasks, and work…

Who we are
&gt;
Atoms is building the machines that power the next era of progress.
&gt;
Over the last decade, software has transformed the digital world. But the physical world, where food is made, minerals are mined, goods are moved, and industries are run, remains far less intelligent, far less efficient, and far more constrained. We&#x27;re changing that.
&gt;
Atoms builds Physical AI- real-world robots for the industries that move civilization forward, starting with food, mining, and transport. Our systems are designed to understand, predict, and control the real world with precision, turning complex physical operations into something more reliable, more scalable, and more productive.
&gt;
This work requires more than robotics. It requires deep integration across hardware, software, AI, operations, manufacturing, and real estate. We don&#x27;t just build machines in a lab. We deploy them into real environments, operate them, learn from them, and improve them until they work at scale.
&gt;
We are roboticists, engineers, operators, and builders. We believe the next great technology companies will not only transform information, but the physical systems that shape everyday life.
&gt;
If you want to work on hard problems with real-world impact, join us.
&gt;
&gt;
What we&#x27;re looking for
&gt;
Actively pursuing a Bachelor/Master in Computer Science, Engineering or a related technical field
&gt;
Graduating in Fall/Winter 2027 or Spring/Summer 2028.
&gt;
3.7 GPA Minimum
&gt;
Must have completed an introductory Computer Science course
&gt;
Have advanced programming experience in one or more application or systems languages (Go, Python, Ruby, Java, Kotlin, C/C++, etc.)
&gt;
A problem-solver who thrives in tackling diverse technical challenges and demonstrates a clear track record of growth and learning
&gt;
A take-charge individual who exhibits ownership and takes pride in writing clean, maintainable, and fun code
&gt;
An engineer who can dive deep into open source software, find issues, and fix them.
&gt;
&gt;
What you&#x27;ll do
&gt;
As…

Celonis is the trusted platform to industrialize Enterprise AI. At our core is the Celonis Context Model - which combines process data, business knowledge, and intelligence into a living digital twin of the enterprise that AI can actually understand, turning AI&#x27;s operational blind spots into operational clarity. World&#x27;s leading companies trust Celonis and its global ecosystem of partners to make their AI agents, people, systems, and processes work together, achieving transformational outcomes. We believe there&#x27;s a massive opportunity to unlock global productivity and sustainability by giving AI the context to understand how every business process really works. Join our mission to make processes work for people, companies, and the planet.
&gt;
&gt; The Team:
&gt;
Celonis Demo Engineering is the creative and technical engine of our Go-To-Market strategy. We are on a high-stakes mission to build the Next-Gen Demo Factory - a world where AI agents and LLMs handle the heavy lifting of demo creation, democratizing demo excellence for 1,000+ GTM colleagues. We create experiences that kick off our customers&#x27; journey with Celonis and help them visualize the future on our platform.
&gt;
To build these experiences, we collaborate with Value Engineering, Product Management, Product Marketing, Enablement, and Industry teams - and we push the limits of the Celonis platform to bring our vision to life.
&gt;
The Role:
&gt;
As a Demo Engineering Intern, you&#x27;ll sit at the intersection of technology, storytelling, and business strategy - and you&#x27;ll contribute to our Next-Gen Demo Factory mission, where AI agents and smart workflows are transforming how we build and deliver demos at scale. You&#x27;ll help prototype agentic tools, configure demos on the Celonis platform, and experiment with AI-assisted storytelling. But this isn&#x27;t just a technical role: you&#x27;ll also develop a broad understanding of the real-world business problems Celonis solves across industries like manufacturing, retail, and financial…

&gt;
About Company
&gt;
Rubrik (NYSE: RBRK) is on a mission to secure the world&#x27;s data. With Zero Trust Data SecurityTM, we help organizations achieve business resilience against cyberattacks, malicious insiders, and operational disruptions. Rubrik Security Cloud, powered by advanced AI and machine learning, secures data across enterprise, cloud, and SaaS applications - combining cyber resilience with generative AI to automate threat hunting, accelerate cyber recovery, and surface real-time data insights. We help organizations uphold data integrity, deliver data availability that withstands adverse conditions, continuously monitor data risks and threats, and restore businesses with their data when infrastructure is attacked.
&gt;
Our Technology
&gt;
Overview of our technology from our Co-founder Soham Mazumdar - Intelligent Data Management Across Clouds
&gt;
Role: Software Engineer Intern - Core UI
&gt;
Join our dynamic Core UI Engineering team to solve immense technical challenges and build award winning UI . Members of this team work on multiple product lines, build state of the art UI Infrastructure, focus on peak performance &amp; AI-driven automation, and enhance our visualization portfolio &amp; design library using TypeScript, React and GraphQL. As an intern, you will have the opportunity to contribute to various projects, learning and growing alongside world-class engineers while heavily leveraging AI coding assistants and automated testing tools in your daily development lifecycle.
&gt;
Requirements:
&gt;
Currently pursuing a Bachelor&#x27;s or Master&#x27;s degree in Computer Science or a related field
&gt;
Strong foundation in Computer Science fundamentals, including data structures, algorithms, and software design principles
&gt;
Passionate about learning new technologies and tools, with a keen interest in front-end development and leveraging AI-assisted development workflows to ship high-quality code faster.
&gt;
&gt;
Good to have:
&gt;
Proficiency in developing and debugging in front-end technologies such…

About HeyGen
&gt;
At HeyGen, our mission is to make visual storytelling accessible to all. Over the last decade, visual content has become the preferred method of information creation, consumption, and retention. But the ability to create such content, in particular videos, continues to be costly and challenging to scale. Our ambition is to build technology that equips more people with the power to reach, captivate, and inspire audiences.
Learn more at www.heygen.com . Visit our Mission and Culture doc here .
&gt;
&gt; The Role
&gt;
HeyGen ships fast, and every release deserves a launch that does it justice. We are looking for a product marketer to own our launches end to end: the calendar, the story, the video, the rollout, and the results. Our launches are X-led, so you will craft the strategy and story that carry each release, then brief every partner and channel, keep Product, Sales, and Marketing moving together, and measure the success. This is a hands-on, full-time, 6-month contract based in San Francisco or Los Angeles, starting January 2027, for someone who can set the strategy and also do the work. Based on performance and business needs, the contract may convert to a permanent role, which could mean leading product marketing for a specific HeyGen product line.
&gt;
What You&#x27;ll Do
&gt;
Own launch strategy and execution - You will run the launch calendar and decide where, when, and how we announce new products. For each priority release, you will craft the story for our X-led launches, defining the audience, positioning, messaging, proof, and success metrics, and scale the rollout to the size of the release.
&gt;
Partner with Product and Research - You will understand each release well before it ships and shape it along the way: advising on product naming, identifying what research we need, and giving feedback on the UI.
&gt;
Lead the launch video - You will take it from concept and script through production and final cut. On bigger launches, a video production team supports…

Summary
&gt;
The individual in this internship role will contribute to the advancement of neutral-atom based quantum computing technologies. ​You will work with our Technical Product Managers to define and coordinate how we are prototyping and building our next generation systems. This role is ideal for someone with a strong technical background relevant to neutral atom quantum computing who is at the same time interested in technical management and cross-functional coordination work.
&gt;
Responsibilities
&gt;
&gt;
Capture technical requirements for hardware / software components of next generation neutral atom quantum computers.
&gt;
&gt;
Compile and organize technical documentation to be easily accessible across the organization.
&gt;
&gt;
Help define hardware testing criteria and test sequences for control software features
&gt;
&gt;
Support planning of technical projects including system builds and associated progress tracking.
&gt;
&gt;
Contribute time to additional projects as directed by your mentor(s).
&gt;
&gt;
Qualifications
&gt;
&gt;
Pursuing a degree in physics, engineering, computer science, mathematics, or a related field.
&gt;
Excellent problem-solving and organizational skills.
&gt;
&gt;
Strong communication and teamwork skills.
&gt;
&gt;
On-site internship. There is no relocation offered for this role.
&gt;
QuEra is committed to cultivating a diverse work environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We highly value diversity in our current and future employees and do not discriminate (including in our hiring and promotion practices) based on race, religion, color, national origin, gender, gender expression, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by law.
&gt;

Summary
&gt;
The Photonics team at QuEra pioneers cutting-edge photonic chips for integration into neutral-atom quantum computers. QuEra Computing Inc. seeks a Photonics Data Engineer Intern to develop an AI-powered data infrastructure that supports our design, fabrication, and testing workflows. You&#x27;ll develop tools that transform raw measurement and metrology data into actionable insights, directly informing how we design better photonic chips faster for large-scale neutral atom quantum computers. We are looking for the Photonics Data Engineer Intern to join us for Winter 2027.
&gt;
Responsibilities
&gt;
AI-powered Data Infrastructure: Develop an AI-powered data management infrastructure for photonic integrated circuit (PIC) design, fabrication, and testing workflows.
&gt;
Automation and Tooling: Write Python functions and utilities to automate data ingestion, cleaning, and organization across multiple data sources.
&gt;
Performance Analysis Pipelines: Build analysis pipelines to extract key device performance metrics (e.g., insertion loss, extinction ratio, bandwidth, yield). Analyze fabrication metrology datasets from multiple foundries and correlate findings with device performance to identify process-performance relationships.
&gt;
Cross-functional Collaboration: Work with other photonics engineers to define data schemas and best practices for reproducible design and testing workflows.
&gt;
Documentation: Document data infrastructure and analysis workflows for long-term team use.
&gt;
Qualifications
&gt;
Currently pursuing or recently completed a Bachelor&#x27;s or Master&#x27;s degree in Computer Science, Physics, Mathematics, or a related discipline.
&gt;
Strong proficiency in Python programming, with hands-on experience using AI and data science libraries including PyTorch, NumPy, SciPy, and Pandas, and familiarity with workflow automation tools.
&gt;
Working knowledge of data storage formats, database design principles, and data analysis and visualization frameworks.
&gt;
Proven track record of…

Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? Coinbase is building the future of finance for people, institutions and their agents, with one place to trade crypto, equities, derivatives and prediction markets, use stablecoins, and connect AI agents with clear controls. The bar is high and the pace is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#x27;t a place for complacency. It&#x27;s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits and do the best work of your career. If you&#x27;re ready to build the future of finance with a championship team who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for in-person working sessions
&gt;
&gt; This is a 12-week internship during summer 2027.
&gt;
Coinbase&#x27;s Application Security team is rethinking how offensive security works. We use frontier AI models to find vulnerabilities at scale, red team our own AI systems, and automate the parts of security work that don&#x27;t need a human. As an intern, you&#x27;ll join that effort on a scoped project and see your work used in real security decisions.
&gt;
What you&#x27;ll do:
&gt;
Build and test tooling that uses frontier AI models to surface vulnerabilities across Coinbase&#x27;s products, working alongside senior engineers on design and review.
&gt;
Help red team internal AI systems - probing for prompt injection, jailbreak attempts, and tool misuse, then documenting what you find and how to fix it.
&gt;
Automate pieces of the vulnerability triage, validation and remediation workflows so the bug bounty, vulnerability response pipelines move faster and become AI native.
&gt;
Reproduce and verify reported vulnerabilities across common classes (OWASP Top 10, SANS Top 25), and write findings that engineering partners can act on.
&gt;
Practice responsible AI use: keep a human in the loop, measure whether your tooling actually improves speed or quality, and be honest when it doesn&#x27;t.
&gt;
Required Skills and Experience:
&gt;
Currently pursuing a…

Eulerity is an AI-native marketing automation platform. Our software runs paid advertising, social, listings, reputation, and call tracking for thousands of locations across enterprise franchises and SMB networks, executing autonomously across Google, Meta, Apple, and Microsoft. The Technical Operations team is the analytical engine that keeps that execution sharp.
&gt;
We are hiring an intern to sit with this team for the Spring 2027 semester.
&gt;
Who we are looking for
This is a marketing internship for someone who loves the numbers side of marketing. We are looking for someone who is genuinely analytical. The kind of person who opens a messy dataset and gets curious instead of overwhelmed. Who enjoys figuring out why a number moved. Who can read a chunk of SQL or Python and follow what it does, even if they would not write it from scratch. Who wants to build a marketing career grounded in data, not just instinct.
&gt;
If you love spreadsheets, you will feel at home here. If you have ever built a model in Excel just to understand something better, even more so.
&gt;
What you will actually do
You will work alongside our Technical Account Management and Analytics teams, supporting the data and analysis side of campaign management. That includes:
&gt;
Supporting campaign performance reviews by pulling data and flagging anything that looks off for the account team to dig into.
&gt;
Updating and maintaining the Excel and Sheets trackers our account teams use day to day, and learning how the models behind them work.
&gt;
Helping with campaign audits across multi-location brands, checking settings, budgets, and tracking against a checklist.
&gt;
Pulling and cleaning performance data from Google Ads, Meta, LinkedIn, and our internal platform for reports and analyses.
&gt;
Testing and documenting new workflows the team is building with AI tools.
&gt;
Pitching in on internal projects, like documentation and process improvements, that make the team run smoother.
&gt;
You will not be writing ad copy or…

XPENG is a leading smart technology company at the forefront of innovation, integrating advanced AI and autonomous driving technologies into its vehicles, including electric vehicles (EVs), electric vertical take-off and landing (eVTOL) aircraft, and robotics. With a strong focus on intelligent mobility, XPENG is dedicated to reshaping the future of transportation through cutting-edge R&amp;D in AI, machine learning, and smart connectivity.
&gt;
&gt;
About the Role
&gt;
We are looking for a new graduate Software Engineer to join XPENG&#x27;s Computing Platform team. We build a unified compute platform that provides core AI infrastructure for autonomous driving, robotics, and intelligent cockpit applications.
&gt;
&gt;
Our platform supports batch and real-time streaming data processing at a scale of hundreds of millions of records per day . It processes data from files, datasets, lakehouse tables, and streaming sources, supporting multimodal workloads across images, videos, point clouds, and sensor streams. Key use cases include data mining , data cleaning, automated captioning and tagging, and embedding generation .
&gt;
Large-scale inference is another core focus of the team, spanning offline batch inference and online model serving. You will help build and optimize infrastructure for deploying and running multimodal and other AI models, including model deployment, request routing, CPU/GPU resource scheduling, autoscaling, and monitoring. The work focuses on improving inference throughput, latency, reliability, and cost efficiency, while making it easier for algorithm teams to bring models into production.
&gt;
&gt;
We are also developing intelligent platform capabilities through reusable agent skills, Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers and integrations, and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG). You will work alongside experienced engineers to build reliable, scalable systems, automate engineering workflows, and improve the developer experience.
&gt;
&gt;
Job Responsibilities
&gt;
Contribute to one or…

ABOUT ROCKET LAB
&gt;
Rocket Lab is the end-to-end space company building rockets, spacecraft, and critical subsystems that keep the world connected, protected, expand humanity&#x27;s reach to the Moon, Mars, and beyond. We move fast, build real hardware for meaningful missions, and make the impossible routine. Come shape the future with us.
&gt;
&gt; SPACE SYSTEMS
&gt;
At Rocket Lab, we&#x27;re not just launching rockets - we&#x27;re building the future of space. Our Space Systems team builds everything from complete spacecraft, precision payloads to the components and subsystems that allow them to thrive in space, like solar panels, flight software, star trackers, optical systems, separation systems, radios, and more.
&gt;
Our Space Systems team has enabled more than 1,700 missions, ranging from interplanetary exploration, in-space manufacturing to national security and defense initiatives. The team has built spacecraft, payloads, and components for missions to the Moon and Mars, working with partners including NASA, the Space Development Agency, and the U.S. Space Force. Whether it&#x27;s a single high-performance spacecraft, constellation, or the vertically integrated components that help them get to space - our world class Space Systems team is empowering some of the boldest and most ambitious space missions.
&gt;
SPACECRAFT PROPULSION COMPONENTS ENGINEER I
&gt;
We&#x27;re currently seeking a Spacecraft Propulsion Components Engineer I for our propulsion engineering team based out of Long Beach, CA. As a Propulsion Components Engineer, you&#x27;re responsible for system-level and component-level ownership of space systems propulsion and fluidic development. This team supports our Space Systems division, and leads cutting-edge programs for civil, commercial, and defense customers.
&gt;
WHAT YOU&#x27;LL GET TO DO:
&gt;
Own development of new or existing products or systems, acting as technical lead to guide team through end-to-end development process.
&gt;
Conceptual and detailed designs in CAD for propulsion system…

Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#x27;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver-The World&#x27;s Most Experienced DriverTM-to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo&#x27;s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.
&gt;
&gt; Software Engineering builds the brains of Waymo&#x27;s fully autonomous driving technology. Our software allows the Waymo Driver to perceive the world around it, make the right decision for every situation, and deliver people safely to their destinations. We think deeply and solve complex technical challenges in areas like robotics, perception, decision-making and deep learning, while collaborating with hardware and systems engineers. If you&#x27;re a software engineer or researcher who&#x27;s curious and passionate about Level 4 autonomous driving, we&#x27;d like to meet you.
&gt;
Waymo interns partner with leaders in the industry on projects that create impact to the company. We believe learning is a two-way street: applying your knowledge while providing you with opportunities to expand your skill-set. Interns are an important part of our culture and our recruiting pipeline. Join us at Waymo for a fun and rewarding internship!
&gt;
&gt;
You will:
&gt;
Work with Waymo&#x27;s SOTA ML models
&gt;
Research novel ways to evaluate the quality and safety of model predictions across prediction heads and modalities
&gt;
Find model evaluation gaps and prototype ways to address them
&gt;
Collaborate with partner teams across Waymo to launch novel eval products which advance business needs
&gt;
&gt;
You have:
&gt;
Currently enrolled…

Lightmatter is leading the revolution in AI data center infrastructure, enabling the next giant leaps in human progress. The company invented the world&#x27;s first 3D-stacked photonics engine, PassageTM, capable of connecting thousands to millions of processors at the speed of light in extreme-scale data centers for the most advanced AI and HPC workloads.
&gt;
Lightmatter raised $400 million in its Series D round, reaching a valuation of $4.4 billion. We will continue to accelerate the development of data center photonics and grow every department at Lightmatter!
&gt;
If you&#x27;re passionate about tackling complex challenges, making an impact, and being an expert in your craft, join our team of brilliant scientists, engineers, and accomplished industry leaders.
&gt;
Lightmatter is (re)inventing the future of computing with light!
&gt;
&gt; About this job
&gt;
Are you ready to do meaningful internship work on technology that is changing how AI systems are built? At Lightmatter you will have mentorship from leaders in photonics and computing. We build photonic interconnect chips designed for large-scale AI compute clusters. As an Embedded Software Engineer for our products. You will develop the control, telemetry, monitoring, and stabilization firmware that maintains the health and lock of our optical transceivers, alongside the tooling required for system bring-up. Collaborating directly with systems, digital, analog, and photonics engineers, you will develop well-defined firmware components through their full lifecycle-from initial requirements to final release-while acquiring deep domain expertise in an emerging field.
&gt;
Responsibilities:
&gt;
Help develop firmware modules for optical transceiver control, telemetry, and monitoring, with guidance from senior engineers.
&gt;
Enhance firmware testing and integration framework development for embedded projects.
&gt;
Incorporate development kit hardware test workflows into the software review and approval process.
&gt;
Write and debug integration tests…

Work Arrangement
&gt;
This is a full-time, on-site position with occasional required travel.
&gt;
Job Overview
&gt;
The Mechanical Engineer I supports the design, development, fabrication, integration, and testing of mechanical components and systems for specialty marine vehicles. Working under the supervision and mentorship of more experienced engineers, this position applies fundamental engineering principles, develops design documentation, and collaborates with fabrication and multidisciplinary engineering teams to deliver reliable equipment for maritime applications.
&gt;
Essential Functions
&gt;
Support team efforts to design, manufacture, integrate, and test mechanical components, structures, and outfitting equipment for submersible maritime systems.
&gt;
Contribute to the development of custom shipboard equipment, including walkways, seating, storage compartments and systems, operator interfaces, and provisions for integrated wiring harnesses and electrical components.
&gt;
Assist with the design, analysis, and integration of mechanical systems, components, structures, and assemblies.
&gt;
Apply engineering fundamentals and established engineering methods to solve straightforward technical challenges under the guidance and mentorship of more experienced engineers.
&gt;
Generate, revise, and manage 3D CAD models, mechanical assemblies, detailed drawings, and fabrication documentation.
&gt;
Assist in developing engineering and design data, including fabrication drawings, system descriptions, diagrams, technical reports, and customer presentations.
&gt;
Support the planning, coordination, and integration of mechanical and electromechanical equipment aboard vessels and vessel mockups.
&gt;
Support prototyping, virtual and physical testing, troubleshooting, and evaluation of components and systems in laboratory, shop, waterfront, and field environments.
&gt;
Assist in planning and executing assigned project tasks, including technical design activities, documentation, schedule tracking, and status…

ABOUT ROCKET LAB
&gt;
Rocket Lab is the end-to-end space company building rockets, spacecraft, and critical subsystems that keep the world connected, protected, expand humanity&#x27;s reach to the Moon, Mars, and beyond. We move fast, build real hardware for meaningful missions, and make the impossible routine. Come shape the future with us.
&gt;
&gt; NEUTRON
&gt;
Neutron is a medium lift launch vehicle capable of delivering the mega constellations of tomorrow, high assurance payloads, and human spaceflight. As a highly reusable launch platform, Neutron will deliver a highly cost-effective and reliable launch solution leveraging Rocket Lab&#x27;s proven execution history with the Electron program. If you&#x27;re interested in joining a high performing team, pushing the boundaries with a clean sheet development of re-usable liquid launch vehicle, this is your opportunity!
&gt;
TEST &amp; LAUNCH OPERATIONS ENGINEER I
&gt;
